## Context
Author clarification, 2026-11-07: interruption means execution stopped with an uncertain outcome for the last outside action. Ordinary pauses, messages, command boundaries, and known-complete actions do not trigger a check.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Raid and hunt's resume paths (also loaded by the coder profile) require reading back an uncertain outside action immediately before retrying that action.
- [ ] No per-command check, new guard, or new rule file is introduced; ordinary pauses and known-complete actions require no extra check.
